From 78e93893ccd1a1881113773236291d9cf3ef8e47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:59:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] dt-bindings: watchdog: arm,sp805: reference the PrimeCell
 binding

The SP805 binding ends in unevaluatedProperties: false but, unlike the
other PrimeCell bindings, never references /schemas/arm/primecell.yaml#,
so arm,primecell-periphid -- the override for the hardware ID value --
cannot be described on an SP805 node. That override is not optional on
hardware that needs it: an SP805 whose ID header is absent never gets
past amba_match() without it and no watchdog exists, and the existing
hix5hd2 board file already carries the property for this reason. Add the
reference.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/arm,sp805.yaml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/arm,sp805.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/watchdog/arm,sp805.yaml
@@ -16,6 +16,7 @@ description: |+
 
 allOf:
   - $ref: /schemas/watchdog/watchdog.yaml#
+  - $ref: /schemas/arm/primecell.yaml#
 
 # Need a custom select here or 'arm,primecell' will match on lots of nodes
 select:
